{"requirements":[{"id":"https_endpoint_8443","requirement":"On node1, a web server serves HTTPS at / on TCP port 8443.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Apache was active and listening on TCP 8443. Direct HTTPS requests returned HTTP 200 both before and after node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-821eb9a539544a9b","cmd-9cc72af78963450c","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"required_root_response","requirement":"The HTTPS root path returns secure-os-comparison-ready.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Requests to https://10.100.91.10:8443/ returned the required body before and after restart; the page hash was also unchanged across the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2ceb5cb1ac824fd0","cmd-821eb9a539544a9b","cmd-9cc72af78963450c"]},{"id":"system_trusted_certificate","requirement":"HTTPS uses a certificate trusted by node1's system trust store.","status":"satisfied","summary":"curl used the system CA bundle, matched the certificate IP SAN, and reported successful certificate verification. Independent openssl verification against the system bundle also succeeded before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3f8d703b4264489e","cmd-821eb9a539544a9b","cmd-9cc72af78963450c"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Task-related installation, certificate creation, trust configuration, firewall configuration, and service enablement had clear roles. The restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service/content were observed. One unnecessary retained side effect was the default wildcard TCP 80 listener created when httpd was started; only 8443 was needed, and it remained after reboot. A minor retained residue was /var/tmp/secure-web.pre-reboot.boot_id: its creation supported bounded restart evidence, but it was not cleaned afterward. No reverted unnecessary mutations were observed. Final package health was clean and no failed services were present.","evidence_ids":["cmd-abb5441a5d694edf","cmd-2ceb5cb1ac824fd0","cmd-17531d4b199443cf","cmd-6f85d8adcf454ec2","cmd-9cc72af78963450c","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The required trusted HTTPS response on TCP 8443 worked before and after a verified node restart. Operational quality was strong, with minor hygiene deductions for the unnecessary port 80 listener and an unremoved reboot-evidence file.","limitations":["HTTPS was tested from node1 to its own managed IP rather than from an independent remote client.","The DNF transaction output was truncated, so every package upgraded as part of dependency resolution cannot be individually audited; the final package-health check was clean."]}
